WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:02.752
Man, I really appreciate
you coming out here,

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:05.338
get a chance to see our facility here.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.173
We got pool.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.091
We got ping pongs.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:11.344
See, we even got like a little
golf simulator over here.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.178
No way. Come on

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.471
It's a little golf simulator over here.

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:14.305
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:15.140
I need to take some pictures.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:15.974
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:17.642
Take them back to the Cardinals.

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.436
It's crazy because last year,

00:00:19.436 --> 00:00:20.770
my first year here with the team,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.398
was the first year they opened
up this practice facility

00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:25.900
and it is unbelievable.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.902
Eat over there food.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.404
Got massage rooms.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.531
You guys sell memberships?

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:39.456
JJ, what's up man?

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:40.290
How are you?

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.124
Sorry. I can't give you my right hand.

00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:42.417
No. Worries. No worries.

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.710
In due time. In due time.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.544
In due time indeed.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.046
I really appreciate you being here.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:46.880
Glad to be here, man.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.966
So first, I just wanna
start off with family.

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.594
Like what was it like
growing up in your household

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:54.304
with all the athletes?

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:56.222
Competitive. Extremely competitive.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.308
Obviously, my two brothers,
both being in the league now.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:00:59.392
Which is sick. Just for the record.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.226
Unbelievable.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.186
You just say that like it's...

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:02.228
It's crazy, man.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.272
It's crazy because we
literally used to play

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:05.190
in the front yard.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.608
Obviously me being the oldest,

00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.485
I used to beat up on
them a bit probably which

00:01:08.485 --> 00:01:11.279
I take credit for turning
them into some athletes.

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:13.448
But it was truly competitive.

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:14.282
It was wild.

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:16.534
My parents started us out in
hockey when we were young.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:17.368
And I truly believe that
one of the reasons...

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:18.787
That’s that Wisconsin thing

00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:19.871
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:21.498
One of the reasons we're successful.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:23.750
So I started skating when
I was three years old.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.751
So when I was three years old,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.252
I was trying to balance myself on ice

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.379
on this little itty bitty blade.

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:32.383
And I think that that taught
me some core strengths.

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:34.219
Some ability to handle my body in space.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:35.053
How to move around,

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:35.887
how to balance,

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:36.805
how to coordinate yourself.

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:37.972
And my brothers and I,

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:38.807
we all played hockey.

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:39.808
That was our number one sport.

00:01:39.808 --> 00:01:40.600
Never knew that.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.768
Ya’ll just wanted to hit people.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.477
-I get it. I get it.
-That's it. That's it.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:43.019
It all makes sense now.

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:44.104
So we were going in the basement.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.022
We'd have these mini sticks
where we'd get on our knees

00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:48.775
and we'd play hockey,
and we'd bang around.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.193
The basement walls took a beating.

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.653
We broke through some basement walls.

00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:53.571
We had to pay for some
dry wall with chores

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:54.489
and things like that.

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:56.908
But always competitive,
always trying to win.

00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:58.368
I didn't take it easy on them.

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:00.870
They'd cry for a second and get back up

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.080
and get back in the game.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.373
It was always competitive.

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:06.751
I can't imagine having one sibling

00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:08.294
being a professional athlete,

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.338
but having all three.

00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:11.214
Like once you got there,

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:15.009
did you sort of know that
they would make it too?

00:02:15.009 --> 00:02:17.720
I knew they would both
make it cause the mindset.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:18.763
I think that...

00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:20.807
We come from a small town in Wisconsin.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:24.018
We had two Division I
football players ever.

00:02:24.018 --> 00:02:26.312
One of them made it to the NFL.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.523
All that did for me was
tell me it was possible.

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:30.024
So I just had to follow a plan,

00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:32.318
and then my brothers
could follow that plan.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.404
I knew their drive and how hard they work

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:35.363
and how determined they were.

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:36.489
I knew they'd make it.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.991
You started off at Central Michigan.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.825
Yeah.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:39.659
Right.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.244
And then you went to Wisconsin.

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:42.078
Yeah.

00:02:42.078 --> 00:02:42.912
As a walk on.

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:44.122
Yeah.

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:44.956
How.

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:48.793
I went to Central Michigan as a tight end.

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:49.627
I was on scholarship.

00:02:49.627 --> 00:02:50.587
I told my parents,

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:51.754
"School's paid for. Don't worry about it."

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:52.589
Right.

00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.090
But they ran the spread offense,

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.009
and I only played like 10 plays a game.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.802
I was a starter my freshman year,

00:02:57.802 --> 00:02:59.679
but I had big dreams. I had big goals.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.973
I didn't wanna play 10 plays a game and...

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.725
That wasn't gonna get me into the NFL.

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:04.934
So I transferred to Wisconsin.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:05.768
I walked on.

00:03:05.768 --> 00:03:08.229
I was like, "I'm gonna put
all my eggs in this basket."

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:09.105
And my parents said

00:03:09.105 --> 00:03:10.690
they had enough money
for one year of school.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.233
If I didn't get a
scholarship after one year,

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:14.027
then I'd have to figure it out on my own.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.904
So I knew I had to make it work.

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:17.488
And sometimes when your
back's against the wall,

00:03:17.488 --> 00:03:20.617
when you don't give yourself
any other option but success,

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:22.327
that's the best way to create success.

00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:23.244
And it worked out.

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:25.872
Yeah. You make that sound real easy.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:26.706
You make it sound real easy,

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.209
but that's unbelievably tough.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.880
And then you actually left
Wisconsin after your junior year.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.714
Yeah.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.590
So how do you...

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.675
You go with no scholarship
and then you leave early.

00:03:37.675 --> 00:03:38.509
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:40.094
Like what did that teach you

00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:41.554
about motivation,

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.224
about betting on yourself, basically?

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.058
That's exactly what...

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:45.975
It was betting on yourself.

00:03:45.975 --> 00:03:46.809
And it was,

00:03:46.809 --> 00:03:49.062
if I put myself in a situation

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.731
where there was no option but to succeed,

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.149
because I literally
would not have been able

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:54.359
to stay going to school.

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:56.277
I literally would not
have been able to advance

00:03:56.277 --> 00:03:57.153
if I didn't do that.

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:59.197
So I was watching a film

00:03:59.197 --> 00:04:00.782
at 10 o'clock 11 o'clock at night

00:04:00.782 --> 00:04:02.617
with the coaches because
I was on the scout team.

00:04:02.617 --> 00:04:03.952
They weren't gonna
watch me during the day,

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:05.119
they had starters to watch.

00:04:05.119 --> 00:04:06.162
So I was on the scout team,

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:07.330
and we were watching film at night.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.539
I was showing up early for work.

00:04:08.539 --> 00:04:09.582
I was with the strength coach.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.042
I was on the scout team.

00:04:11.042 --> 00:04:11.960
I was going up against

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.670
the number one offensive
line in Wisconsin.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.129
We had like six, All Americans.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.756
Our backup was an All American

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.383
by the time he was a senior high.

00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:20.468
I was going up against the
best guys in the country.

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:21.719
And I was like, "If I can
play against these guys,

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:23.388
I can play against anybody."

00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:25.723
And it was every single day,

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:27.850
like, I'd get my ass kicked.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:30.019
But then I'd get up and I'd
kick somebody else's ass.

00:04:30.019 --> 00:04:32.105
And then once I'd kick
in All American's ass,

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.524
I was like, "Maybe I'm an
All American. Hang on."

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:35.441
And then I'd be like,

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.485
"Maybe I'm a draft pick." And...

00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:40.154
You left to go to the NFL
after your junior year.

00:04:40.154 --> 00:04:40.989
Right.

00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:42.490
How did that decision come about?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.034
I mean, I'd be lying to
you if I didn't say that

00:04:45.034 --> 00:04:47.245
the fact that you get paid
to do the thing you love

00:04:47.245 --> 00:04:48.246
wasn't a part of it too.

00:04:48.246 --> 00:04:49.580
Like they told me,

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.500
you submit your forms to see
if you were gonna get drafted.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.002
Like when you're a junior,
you submit the forms.

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:56.296
And they said that I might
be a late first round

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.131
or early second rounder.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.465
So my coaches there were telling me

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:00.925
that I might be a third rounder.

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:02.593
They're trying to get
you to stay in school.

00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:03.428
They're trying to get me in school.

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:04.262
That's not all.

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:05.096
Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:05.096 --> 00:05:08.182
So I was like, "I know I'm
gonna crush the combine.

00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:09.642
I know that my film has been good.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.019
I know I'm gonna interview good."

00:05:11.019 --> 00:05:12.186
So I'd bet myself again.

00:05:12.186 --> 00:05:12.979
I'd bet myself.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.773
Went to the combine, had
a really good combine.

00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:17.692
Ended up getting drafted 11th overall.

00:05:17.692 --> 00:05:19.944
And I knew that I would
have an opportunity

00:05:19.944 --> 00:05:23.197
to potentially set up my
family for generations to come.

00:05:23.197 --> 00:05:27.201
And the risks of not having that happen,

00:05:27.201 --> 00:05:29.787
I couldn't take those risks.

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:31.456
That's amazing.

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:32.290
You want me to show you
the facility real quick?

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:33.124
I do. Yeah.

00:05:33.124 --> 00:05:36.836
Let's check it out. This
place is incredible.

00:05:38.629 --> 00:05:39.630
This place is insane.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.465
Yeah, man.

00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:41.299
So it's crazy.

00:05:41.299 --> 00:05:42.800
Like it's so nice.

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:47.347
You don't get with so much
use out of it up here.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:48.639
Everything's big man friendly too.

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:49.474
It's got big chairs.

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:50.016
Exactly.

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:50.600
It's got big couches.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.017
Everything.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.810
Yeah. This is nice.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.145
It's designed pretty well too.

00:05:54.145 --> 00:05:54.979
It is.

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:55.813
It has nice features.

00:05:55.813 --> 00:05:56.731
Perfect spot.

00:05:56.731 --> 00:06:00.026
Yeah. Craziest thing
though, about this facility.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:00.860
And I still...

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.196
I need to ask Sarver why he did it.

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.822
There's a hot tub out there, man.

00:06:04.822 --> 00:06:06.741
I was wondering why there's
no wall right there.

00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:07.575
There's a hot tub...

00:06:07.575 --> 00:06:08.409
Look out the road?

00:06:08.409 --> 00:06:10.453
There's a real hot tub
that faces the road.

00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:12.121
You gotta talk to Sarver about that.

00:06:12.121 --> 00:06:13.623
Just put you and D. Bookie

00:06:13.623 --> 00:06:14.749
and all the guys out there

00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:17.043
and you can just chill in the hot tub.

00:06:18.336 --> 00:06:19.837
So at one point,

00:06:20.838 --> 00:06:22.590
aside from quarterbacks
or anything like that,

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:25.009
you was the highest earner in the league.

00:06:25.009 --> 00:06:26.636
How did you deal...

00:06:26.636 --> 00:06:30.306
Not did or do, you deal
with the wealth? Right?

00:06:30.306 --> 00:06:31.140
Yeah.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:31.974
I don't know what your bank account

00:06:31.974 --> 00:06:32.975
or account looked like in college,

00:06:32.975 --> 00:06:36.396
but I had 151 dollars before I got drafted.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:37.230
Oh man.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.648
Before I declared.

00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:40.900
We went to a bowl game once in college

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.110
and one of my teammates,

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.945
we were gonna go to a party that night.

00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:45.655
And we went to like the foot locker

00:06:45.655 --> 00:06:46.489
and he was like,

00:06:46.489 --> 00:06:48.366
"You gotta get those Jordans
for the party night."

00:06:48.366 --> 00:06:51.119
And I was like, "Those
Jordans are like $300.

00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:52.161
Where am I gonna get that?"

00:06:52.161 --> 00:06:53.704
And he was like, "You got per diem money."

00:06:53.704 --> 00:06:56.082
And I was like, "Yes, I
have $300 of per diem money.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:58.084
You want me to spend it
all on these Jordans?"

00:06:58.084 --> 00:06:59.627
He convinced me. I bought them.

00:06:59.627 --> 00:07:00.962
I bought the Jordans. I had no food.

00:07:00.962 --> 00:07:03.214
I had to find my food
for the rest of the week.

00:07:03.214 --> 00:07:04.048
But I was like, I did it.

00:07:04.048 --> 00:07:06.926
So my financials is a lot different now.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.511
And it's...

00:07:08.511 --> 00:07:09.679
You're figuring it out as you're going.

00:07:09.679 --> 00:07:12.598
and you're putting your own spin on it.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.892
I was always gonna be
conservative of my money

00:07:14.892 --> 00:07:16.477
because I want it to last forever.

00:07:16.477 --> 00:07:19.564
Beyond me for generations to come.

00:07:19.564 --> 00:07:22.525
But I also try and let myself understand

00:07:22.525 --> 00:07:24.444
that you should appreciate and enjoy

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:26.404
what you've worked so hard to get.

00:07:26.404 --> 00:07:27.947
So I'm fortunate here.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:30.074
I live in a beautiful
house here, but I also,

00:07:30.074 --> 00:07:31.576
at the same time I drive a truck

00:07:31.576 --> 00:07:35.163
because I found a way
to get a truck for free.

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:38.416
I don't drive like a crazy fancy car,

00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:39.709
I'm very lucky and I'm fortunate,

00:07:39.709 --> 00:07:42.044
but I am conscious always
of trying to make sure

00:07:42.044 --> 00:07:44.130
that I'm being smart with it

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.089
and not getting crazy.

00:07:45.089 --> 00:07:45.923
And also setting a good example

00:07:45.923 --> 00:07:47.049
for my brothers as well.

00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:49.260
Do you remember what
the best piece of advice

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.054
you were given as far as financially?

00:07:52.054 --> 00:07:54.474
Early on, I always tried to
live off of just endorsements.

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.517
I know that there's plenty of...

00:07:56.517 --> 00:07:58.478
I'm a defensive lineman,

00:07:58.478 --> 00:07:59.312
so there weren't too
many of them early on,

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:01.189
so I wasn't leaving that high off it.

00:08:01.189 --> 00:08:02.732
But that is something
that throughout my career,

00:08:02.732 --> 00:08:04.775
I've always tried and made sure

00:08:04.775 --> 00:08:06.527
that I was bringing enough off the field.

00:08:06.527 --> 00:08:08.488
If I didn't want to,

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.781
I would never have to touch
the on the field stuff.

00:08:10.781 --> 00:08:12.742
So like what advice would you give to a

00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:14.660
young guy coming into the league now

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.454
that you've been in
the league a long time?

00:08:16.454 --> 00:08:19.373
The best advice that I
ever give to young guys is

00:08:19.373 --> 00:08:22.960
invest in yourself, in your
body, in your craft right now

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.086
that you you will never,

00:08:24.086 --> 00:08:25.838
unless you're a absolute genius,

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.882
brilliant business mind,

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:29.759
or you have some unbelievable connections,

00:08:29.759 --> 00:08:32.595
you will never have an
opportunity to earn as much money

00:08:32.595 --> 00:08:34.847
for what we're about to do right now.

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:35.681
Like imagine...

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:36.516
Think about some of the contracts

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:37.517
that are going on right now.

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.185
Think about quarterbacks that are making

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:41.896
$200 plus million dollars in the NFL.

00:08:41.896 --> 00:08:44.023
You have an opportunity to
set yourself up with wealth

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.359
that will last for generations to come.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:47.777
Don't worry about the lifestyle.

00:08:47.777 --> 00:08:50.488
Don't worry about
everything else on the side.

00:08:50.488 --> 00:08:52.240
Worry about what can make you,

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.366
A, maker team great,

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:56.744
but also B, set yourself up financially.

00:08:56.744 --> 00:08:58.829
It's a very difficult thing
because I've been there too.

00:08:58.829 --> 00:09:00.248
I was young. I was a young guy.

00:09:00.248 --> 00:09:02.166
I know that the lifestyle
is extremely enticing.

00:09:02.166 --> 00:09:03.251
I know that there's...

00:09:03.251 --> 00:09:05.545
And I'm not saying you
gotta commit to it 24/7,

00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:08.339
like you have to be psychotic about it.

00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:10.675
But you do kind of gotta
be psychotic about it.

00:09:10.675 --> 00:09:11.801
It's always the same.

00:09:11.801 --> 00:09:13.094
Keep the main thing, the main thing.

00:09:13.094 --> 00:09:13.928
Amen.

00:09:13.928 --> 00:09:15.179
Right. And...

00:09:16.264 --> 00:09:17.640
You're giving me flashbacks here, man.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.976
Do you remember what the
first thing was you bought?

00:09:19.976 --> 00:09:22.103
What was your first big purchase?

00:09:22.103 --> 00:09:23.396
I remember my...

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:24.981
The house I bought in Houston.

00:09:24.981 --> 00:09:25.982
Closing the house,

00:09:25.982 --> 00:09:27.608
took the key, drove to the house,

00:09:27.608 --> 00:09:30.152
walked through the front door,
walked through the back door,

00:09:30.152 --> 00:09:32.029
jumped in the pool with all my clothes on.

00:09:32.029 --> 00:09:34.240
Because I was like, I've never...

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.449
I didn't ever think I'd...

00:09:35.449 --> 00:09:36.742
I couldn't conceptualize
having my own house.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:37.743
No greater feeling.

00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:39.704
And I was like, "This is mine."

00:09:39.704 --> 00:09:42.373
I just jumped in my own
pool. I just jumped...

00:09:42.373 --> 00:09:43.958
That was the coolest thing ever for me.

00:09:43.958 --> 00:09:45.418
And then being able to buy my mom a car,

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:48.004
being able to buy my parents a house.

00:09:48.004 --> 00:09:48.838
There's no feeling like that.

00:09:48.838 --> 00:09:49.714
There's no feeling.

00:09:49.714 --> 00:09:51.215
People probably see me wouldn't know

00:09:51.215 --> 00:09:55.511
that I used to have a
Escalade with 26 inch rims.

00:09:55.511 --> 00:09:56.304
Spinning rims.

00:09:56.304 --> 00:09:59.140
I had a drop down TV in it
and all that stuff, man.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:02.018
But you get a chance
to live and you learn.

00:10:02.018 --> 00:10:02.852
No doubt.

00:10:02.852 --> 00:10:03.686
Yeah.

00:10:03.686 --> 00:10:05.313
Dude, that was like the dream car.

00:10:05.313 --> 00:10:06.147
What?

00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:07.857
That was the dream for a little while

00:10:07.857 --> 00:10:08.691
Them Sprewells

00:10:08.691 --> 00:10:11.319
I had to have them, them spinning wheels.

00:10:11.319 --> 00:10:14.280
Can you remember making
any investment mistakes?

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:16.824
Because I think whenever you
talk to people about money,

00:10:16.824 --> 00:10:18.200
which is so crazy,

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.619
I always ask...

00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.203
I do grassroots basketball. Right?

00:10:21.203 --> 00:10:22.538
So AAU programs.

00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:25.625
I always pick a kid in the room and I say,

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.627
"What would you do with
a million dollars?"

00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:28.753
And it's always the kid

00:10:28.753 --> 00:10:30.921
who thinks that they're
giving the smart answer

00:10:30.921 --> 00:10:33.507
and they be like, "Well,
I'm gonna invest it."

00:10:33.507 --> 00:10:36.218
Well, you don't always
make money when you invest.

00:10:36.218 --> 00:10:39.388
Have you ever had any
situations where you're like,

00:10:39.388 --> 00:10:40.973
"Man, I wish I wouldn't have did that."

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:42.141
But you learned from it.

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:43.434
Right.

00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:47.188
I haven't had any big,
massive mistakes yet

00:10:47.188 --> 00:10:48.898
in terms of losses, like of money.

00:10:48.898 --> 00:10:50.858
I mean, I'm always gonna invest an amount

00:10:50.858 --> 00:10:54.820
that if it went to zero
immediately I'd be safe.

00:10:55.863 --> 00:10:57.990
But the one thing that I am frustrated by

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.700
is there's this company
called Athletic Brewing.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:01.577
It's a non-alcoholic brewing company.

00:11:01.577 --> 00:11:03.913
And I had a chance to get in very early.

00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:05.498
I'm talking very early.

00:11:05.498 --> 00:11:06.666
And I sat there and I was talking

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:09.377
about non-alcoholic beer,
and I'm from Wisconsin.

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:10.252
Everybody in Wisconsin drinks.

00:11:10.252 --> 00:11:11.128
Yeah, that's great.

00:11:11.128 --> 00:11:12.004
So I'm like,

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:14.048
I got my buddies and I'm
bouncing the idea off them.

00:11:14.048 --> 00:11:16.175
And they're like, "Why the
hell would anybody drink beer

00:11:16.175 --> 00:11:17.134
with no alcohol?"

00:11:17.134 --> 00:11:19.387
And I was like, "I don't
know but these numbers

00:11:19.387 --> 00:11:23.015
look really good, man.
People are buying it."

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:26.560
But like I convinced myself not
to do it in the early round.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.522
And a year later it was 3X, 4X.

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:31.190
And I got in the next round,

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:33.317
I always kicked myself about
not believing in myself.

00:11:33.317 --> 00:11:34.985
That's definitely happened to me before.

00:11:34.985 --> 00:11:35.820
Oh man.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.530
And you just sort of gotta let it go.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.448
And sometimes you look
at your financial advisor

00:11:39.448 --> 00:11:40.282
and you say,

00:11:40.282 --> 00:11:41.200
"It's your fault."

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.118
"It's your fault."

00:11:42.118 --> 00:11:45.246
And the problem was, I had
somebody that was telling me,

00:11:45.246 --> 00:11:46.497
"You gotta do it. You gotta do it."

00:11:46.497 --> 00:11:47.373
And I shoved them off.

00:11:47.373 --> 00:11:48.207
And now I have to

00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:50.543
look them in the eyes cause
they went in on the first one

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:51.377
and I gotta apologize.

00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:52.586
Be like, "You're right."

00:11:52.586 --> 00:11:56.549
So for you over your years in the league,

00:11:56.549 --> 00:11:58.884
you done got a ton of awards.

00:11:58.884 --> 00:12:02.179
What do you think you're
the most proud of?

00:12:02.179 --> 00:12:04.432
It has to be the Walter
Payton Man of the Year award

00:12:04.432 --> 00:12:07.143
because that's the one that

00:12:07.143 --> 00:12:09.937
hundreds of thousands of
millions of people helped me get.

00:12:09.937 --> 00:12:10.771
It wasn't me.

00:12:10.771 --> 00:12:13.983
It's not me. I mean,
I was the facilitator.

00:12:13.983 --> 00:12:15.484
I started the fundraiser for Harvey

00:12:15.484 --> 00:12:18.446
and I was the guy who coordinated it.

00:12:18.446 --> 00:12:19.739
But it was people like you.

00:12:19.739 --> 00:12:22.324
It was people like the
kids from Pennsylvania

00:12:22.324 --> 00:12:23.534
that had a lemonade stand

00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:24.994
that sent in their money to the charity.

00:12:24.994 --> 00:12:27.455
It was people from Germany and London

00:12:27.455 --> 00:12:29.081
and people from all over sending it.

00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:30.374
So it wasn't me.

00:12:30.374 --> 00:12:31.834
That's the award that feels like

00:12:31.834 --> 00:12:33.794
the community helped me get the most.

00:12:33.794 --> 00:12:37.465
The fact that you raised over $40 million,

00:12:38.507 --> 00:12:39.800
how did that impact you?

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:40.801
How did that change you?

00:12:40.801 --> 00:12:42.386
When I started the fundraiser,

00:12:42.386 --> 00:12:45.890
I literally was trying to raise $100,000.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.183
I put $100,000 of my own, and I said,

00:12:47.183 --> 00:12:49.018
"I wanna raise $100,000 to match it."

00:12:49.018 --> 00:12:51.395
And the first celebrity,
the first famous person,

00:12:51.395 --> 00:12:54.648
the first person to call
me was you with a donation.

00:12:54.648 --> 00:12:56.400
And I'll tell people
that in every interview

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.359
for the rest of my life,

00:12:57.359 --> 00:13:00.905
that you set off the
foundation for everybody else.

00:13:00.905 --> 00:13:03.532
And we raised over $40 million.

00:13:03.532 --> 00:13:04.366
And it was insane.

00:13:04.366 --> 00:13:07.077
People from all over the country,

00:13:07.077 --> 00:13:11.207
all over the world were donating
and showing their support.

00:13:11.207 --> 00:13:12.082
It was an experience

00:13:12.082 --> 00:13:13.834
I will never experience again in my life.

00:13:13.834 --> 00:13:15.336
And I hope that we
never have to go through

00:13:15.336 --> 00:13:16.295
things like that again.

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:19.507
But never have I had more hope in humanity

00:13:19.507 --> 00:13:21.008
than I had during that time.

00:13:21.008 --> 00:13:22.927
The communities that we play in

00:13:22.927 --> 00:13:24.011
are who support us.

00:13:24.011 --> 00:13:26.764
So when I saw all the
work that you was doing,

00:13:26.764 --> 00:13:28.724
I was inspired.

00:13:28.724 --> 00:13:31.602
I'm forever grateful for
everything that you did there, man.

00:13:31.602 --> 00:13:33.354
It was a wild time,

00:13:33.354 --> 00:13:34.730
and it was...

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:35.898
Man, you don't wanna talk about hectic.

00:13:35.898 --> 00:13:38.943
That was the most hectic
couple of months ever.

00:13:38.943 --> 00:13:40.528
We were in the middle of training camp

00:13:40.528 --> 00:13:41.862
and we were...

00:13:41.862 --> 00:13:43.364
I'd have practice and
meetings during the day.

00:13:43.364 --> 00:13:47.576
And then at night we'd
be meeting with charities

00:13:47.576 --> 00:13:50.663
and politicians and FEMA, and Red Cross.

00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:52.289
And we're trying to figure out...

00:13:52.289 --> 00:13:53.123
Figure out where to go.

00:13:53.123 --> 00:13:53.958
Figure out exactly how to do it

00:13:53.958 --> 00:13:55.876
and to make sure that you're
doing it properly, man.

00:13:55.876 --> 00:13:57.378
It was a wild time.

00:13:57.378 --> 00:13:59.380
It's something I hope I never
have to go through again.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.715
But I also learned so much from it.

00:14:01.715 --> 00:14:02.508
And we helped so many people

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:04.468
because of the generosity of others.

00:14:04.468 --> 00:14:07.012
And while everyone remembers that,

00:14:07.012 --> 00:14:09.181
it started for you in college, right?

00:14:09.181 --> 00:14:10.724
You started your JJ Watt Foundation

00:14:10.724 --> 00:14:12.059
when you were in college.

00:14:12.059 --> 00:14:12.893
Yeah.

00:14:12.893 --> 00:14:15.229
And one of your biggest mottos is

00:14:15.229 --> 00:14:17.398
"Dream big, work hard." right?

00:14:17.398 --> 00:14:18.983
You believe that's what
it takes to succeed.

00:14:18.983 --> 00:14:20.276
Yeah.

00:14:20.276 --> 00:14:21.110
My parents taught me

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.903
from an early age to have big dreams.

00:14:22.903 --> 00:14:24.947
They always said, "Feel free to dream big.

00:14:24.947 --> 00:14:28.534
Feel free to think about
whatever you want to be,

00:14:28.534 --> 00:14:29.785
but you have to be willing to work hard.

00:14:29.785 --> 00:14:31.829
You have to be willing
to make the sacrifices

00:14:31.829 --> 00:14:33.747
and have the discipline."

00:14:33.747 --> 00:14:36.208
My role model for the
charity was Myron Rolle.

00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:37.793
He was at Florida State Safety

00:14:37.793 --> 00:14:39.962
and he started a charity
while he was in college.

00:14:39.962 --> 00:14:42.172
And I remember watching the story on ESPN,

00:14:42.172 --> 00:14:44.508
and they were talking
about him and his story.

00:14:44.508 --> 00:14:47.636
And I was like, "Man, how
was he even smart enough

00:14:47.636 --> 00:14:50.306
to know how to start a charity
while he is in college?"

00:14:50.306 --> 00:14:51.390
So then I started researching it,

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.391
talking to law school,

00:14:52.391 --> 00:14:54.310
and they helped me start a
charity while I was in college.

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.812
And Myron to this day
is a role model of mine.

00:14:56.812 --> 00:14:58.981
Now he's a Rhode scholar and a doctor

00:14:58.981 --> 00:14:59.815
and he's one of the most
brilliant people out there.

00:14:59.815 --> 00:15:02.067
Everything. Everything.

00:15:02.067 --> 00:15:03.944
This is super-duper than ours.

00:15:03.944 --> 00:15:05.571
Take you down, and show you
what the court look like.

00:15:05.571 --> 00:15:06.405
Yes.

00:15:08.032 --> 00:15:11.410
Coolest thing about this
is having the women's team.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.453
Yeah.

00:15:12.453 --> 00:15:13.454
Because there's times

00:15:13.454 --> 00:15:16.415
where we'll be in the weight room

00:15:16.415 --> 00:15:19.084
and Skylar Diggins will
come in there lifting,

00:15:19.084 --> 00:15:20.586
DT would be in there lifting,
you know what I mean?

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.546
Yeah, that's cool. Yeah.

00:15:22.546 --> 00:15:24.840
I think it was after we played the Bucks.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:27.217
We played somebody, and we had an off day.

00:15:27.217 --> 00:15:31.430
And so they had just got
Tina Charles on their team,

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.599
and I came to the gym
just to come see Tina

00:15:33.599 --> 00:15:34.433
because I knew her.

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:36.185
And the music was on.

00:15:37.019 --> 00:15:39.813
Guys from my team were shooting here.

00:15:39.813 --> 00:15:41.273
Some of the women were shooting over there

00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:42.483
and it's just like one big family.

00:15:42.483 --> 00:15:43.400
That's cool. Right?

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.234
Yeah.

00:15:45.235 --> 00:15:47.488
That's special. Two badass teams too.

00:15:47.488 --> 00:15:48.322
Right.

00:15:48.322 --> 00:15:49.156
You was guys have been crushing it.

00:15:49.156 --> 00:15:50.324
We might as well scrimmage, shoot.

00:15:50.324 --> 00:15:51.992
Crushing it. Right?

00:15:51.992 --> 00:15:53.410
That is super-duper nice

00:15:54.244 --> 00:15:55.496
Your wife is a professional soccer player.

00:15:55.496 --> 00:15:56.330
Yeah.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.164
She's awesome, man.

00:15:57.164 --> 00:15:57.998
She's incredible.

00:15:57.998 --> 00:16:01.543
What do you think is going
to take to get female women,

00:16:01.543 --> 00:16:04.421
professional sports,
more and more notoriety?

00:16:04.421 --> 00:16:06.674
I think the more people talk about it,

00:16:06.674 --> 00:16:09.093
the more people watch it,
the more people show up.

00:16:09.093 --> 00:16:11.095
I mean, you obviously
do an unbelievable job

00:16:11.095 --> 00:16:13.514
with showing up to the WNBA.

00:16:13.514 --> 00:16:15.641
My wife and I will sit around
the dinner table at night,

00:16:15.641 --> 00:16:17.184
and we'll talk about the NWSL,

00:16:17.184 --> 00:16:19.436
and we'll talk about,
how can this be bigger?

00:16:19.436 --> 00:16:22.314
Is there a team that we
can buy or invest in?

00:16:22.314 --> 00:16:25.776
Is there a way that we
can influx capital into it

00:16:25.776 --> 00:16:26.610
to make it work?

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:27.736
Is capital the answer?

00:16:27.736 --> 00:16:29.655
Is there a way the viewership
needs to get better

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:32.783
by creating a grounds roots?

00:16:32.783 --> 00:16:33.659
If I had the answer,

00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:34.493
I would do it immediately.

00:16:34.493 --> 00:16:35.327
Right, right.

00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:37.830
But I know the conversations
are the most fun to have

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:41.458
because you know it's coming,

00:16:41.458 --> 00:16:43.210
and it's just a matter of how we continue

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.129
to prop it up and build it up.

00:16:45.129 --> 00:16:46.922
What do you think is next

00:16:46.922 --> 00:16:48.841
as far as like investments or what not?

00:16:48.841 --> 00:16:50.634
Like what you're gonna invest in,

00:16:50.634 --> 00:16:51.552
but what do you think?

00:16:51.552 --> 00:16:53.053
Yeah, I really enjoy investing.

00:16:53.053 --> 00:16:55.097
I think it's another way to be competitive

00:16:55.097 --> 00:16:56.098
outside of the field.

00:16:56.098 --> 00:16:57.683
You can look through decks

00:16:57.683 --> 00:16:59.143
and you can try and pick them apart

00:16:59.143 --> 00:17:00.936
and try and see where the fakes are

00:17:00.936 --> 00:17:02.479
and where the real quality things are.

00:17:02.479 --> 00:17:04.606
And then it's also things
you're passionate about.

00:17:04.606 --> 00:17:06.734
I have been looking at team ownership

00:17:06.734 --> 00:17:09.361
to see if that's something
that's a possibility for me.

00:17:09.361 --> 00:17:11.822
Not in the sense that I
just wanna slap my name

00:17:11.822 --> 00:17:14.158
on a 1% of a team and be like,

00:17:14.158 --> 00:17:15.034
"Hey, look at me. I'm part owner."

00:17:15.034 --> 00:17:15.868
You wanna be involved.

00:17:15.868 --> 00:17:16.702
I wanna be involved.

00:17:16.702 --> 00:17:18.662
I want to be trying to
help make those decisions,

00:17:18.662 --> 00:17:20.539
and use the athlete's perspective

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:25.502
to give what I think can
benefit the organization.

00:17:25.502 --> 00:17:26.420
I think it would be really cool

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:29.298
if that space was in the women's space.

00:17:29.298 --> 00:17:30.174
What year are you?

00:17:30.174 --> 00:17:31.341
11.

00:17:31.341 --> 00:17:32.176
11.

00:17:32.176 --> 00:17:33.010
12.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.261
This is 17, right?

00:17:34.261 --> 00:17:35.095
That's crazy.

00:17:35.095 --> 00:17:35.971
17.

00:17:35.971 --> 00:17:39.475
So what's crazy is, you want to love...

00:17:39.475 --> 00:17:42.853
Especially playing for that long, and...

00:17:42.853 --> 00:17:45.856
What? 12 is real, real long in the NFL.

00:17:45.856 --> 00:17:48.400
So playing for this
long, you want to enjoy.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:49.234
Yeah.

00:17:49.234 --> 00:17:50.903
If I'm gonna be away from my family...

00:17:50.903 --> 00:17:52.237
Yes. I better enjoy it.

00:17:52.237 --> 00:17:53.072
Exactly.

00:17:54.198 --> 00:17:56.366
Have you ever thought about...

00:17:56.366 --> 00:17:57.326
I'm not asking you to retire,

00:17:57.326 --> 00:17:58.869
but do you ever think about that

00:17:58.869 --> 00:18:02.081
as far as like head injuries
and trauma and stuff like that?

00:18:02.081 --> 00:18:04.041
Have you ever thought about like...

00:18:04.041 --> 00:18:07.920
Yeah, I've definitely
thought about retirement.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:12.007
I think I probably thought
about it too early at one point.

00:18:12.007 --> 00:18:13.801
I started thinking about

00:18:13.801 --> 00:18:17.429
the possibility of that when I was 26,

00:18:17.429 --> 00:18:20.057
just because you know
you can't play forever

00:18:20.057 --> 00:18:22.601
and you start to consider
when that day might come.

00:18:22.601 --> 00:18:25.938
But I also on the flip side of that,

00:18:25.938 --> 00:18:28.315
every time that it ever
creeps into my head,

00:18:28.315 --> 00:18:29.441
I'm a competitor, man.

00:18:29.441 --> 00:18:30.484
I'm a competitor and I wanna win.

00:18:30.484 --> 00:18:31.318
I can see.

00:18:31.318 --> 00:18:33.654
And I wanna leave this game
with a damn trophy. And...

00:18:33.654 --> 00:18:34.488
I respect that.

00:18:34.488 --> 00:18:35.948
And there's still stuff

00:18:35.948 --> 00:18:38.367
that I feel like I'm capable
of doing and accomplishing

00:18:38.367 --> 00:18:39.701
and being, and leading.

00:18:39.701 --> 00:18:43.122
And I don't ever wanna look back and say,

00:18:43.122 --> 00:18:44.623
"Man, I wish I would've."

00:18:44.623 --> 00:18:45.916
Or, "I wish I could've."

00:18:45.916 --> 00:18:48.585
And the injuries, and the
things that come with the game.

00:18:48.585 --> 00:18:52.631
I've dealt with them
more than I wish I would.

00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:53.465
Right.

00:18:53.465 --> 00:18:54.716
But I know...

00:18:56.176 --> 00:18:57.511
I know the consequence

00:18:57.511 --> 00:18:59.805
and I know what the possibility is.

00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:03.392
And I'm willing to accept
that right now to keep going.

00:19:03.392 --> 00:19:04.226
And once that...

00:19:04.226 --> 00:19:05.352
Once that line crosses,

00:19:05.352 --> 00:19:07.729
and it flips to where I'm
not willing to accept it,

00:19:07.729 --> 00:19:08.689
that'll be the day.

00:19:08.689 --> 00:19:11.775
But right now I'm willing to
accept the pain and everything.

00:19:11.775 --> 00:19:13.443
Try to get to glory.

00:19:13.443 --> 00:19:15.237
I respect the hell outta that too.

00:19:15.237 --> 00:19:16.905
I do. I do.

00:19:16.905 --> 00:19:18.198
And it's always...

00:19:18.198 --> 00:19:19.032
What about you?

00:19:19.032 --> 00:19:19.867
I wanna ask you the same question.

00:19:19.867 --> 00:19:21.118
I don't know if you're
answering it for me .

00:19:21.118 --> 00:19:22.411
No, I will.

00:19:22.411 --> 00:19:24.037
And it's funny.

00:19:24.037 --> 00:19:28.333
I still love to play like
it's like my rookie year,

00:19:28.333 --> 00:19:29.835
like when I was five years old.

00:19:29.835 --> 00:19:32.254
And I live away from my family.

00:19:32.254 --> 00:19:34.256
And just about every day

00:19:35.424 --> 00:19:38.802
when I wake up and I'm not
there with my wife and my kids.

00:19:38.802 --> 00:19:42.055
I'm like, man, is this really worth it?

00:19:42.055 --> 00:19:43.599
Right.

00:19:43.599 --> 00:19:44.558
And I mean,

00:19:44.558 --> 00:19:48.020
I got friends that aren't
playing, friends that are retired,

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:50.230
that I talk to about it all the time.

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:52.232
And they always tell me,

00:19:52.232 --> 00:19:53.901
"You know what, it's gonna
be one day when you wake up

00:19:53.901 --> 00:19:55.694
and you really can't play.

00:19:55.694 --> 00:19:57.654
And if you still love the game like that,

00:19:57.654 --> 00:19:59.364
then you gotta play."

00:19:59.364 --> 00:20:00.991
And I think my kids and my wife,

00:20:00.991 --> 00:20:04.786
I don't think they would like
who I would be if I was home

00:20:04.786 --> 00:20:06.914
and I can't play basketball.

00:20:06.914 --> 00:20:09.958
I still love it too much.

00:20:09.958 --> 00:20:10.792
Right.

00:20:10.792 --> 00:20:13.587
Right. And if that does
change, like you said...

00:20:13.587 --> 00:20:15.047
That's the other question though,

00:20:15.047 --> 00:20:16.715
is that when that day does come.

00:20:16.715 --> 00:20:19.218
You've spent 20 plus years.

00:20:19.218 --> 00:20:20.052
Listen...

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:20.886
It's gonna be...

00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:21.720
JJ, I don't care...

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:22.554
What's it gonna look like?

00:20:22.554 --> 00:20:25.933
How many investments I
have or anything like that.

00:20:25.933 --> 00:20:27.517
I'm worried about that day.

00:20:27.517 --> 00:20:29.019
No question. I'm with you.

00:20:29.019 --> 00:20:30.395
I'm very much worried about that day.

00:20:30.395 --> 00:20:31.230
I'm with you.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.690
And well, when that day's
come, I'm gonna call you.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:36.276
You can call me, but we
gonna have to talk about it.

00:20:36.276 --> 00:20:37.110
Well, we'll do something together.

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:37.945
Exactly.

00:20:37.945 --> 00:20:38.779
Like golf or something.

00:20:38.779 --> 00:20:39.613
Exactly.

00:20:39.613 --> 00:20:41.949
Speaking of risk, you hosted SNL.

00:20:41.949 --> 00:20:42.783
Yeah.

00:20:42.783 --> 00:20:43.825
You hosted SNL.

00:20:43.825 --> 00:20:46.328
How was that? And like,
is there any parallel

00:20:46.328 --> 00:20:48.747
to live television in sports?

00:20:49.873 --> 00:20:50.832
It was cool, man.

00:20:50.832 --> 00:20:53.418
It was the best. It was a wild week.

00:20:53.418 --> 00:20:57.130
It was a wild experience,
but it was an absolute blast.

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.715
I mean, I'm an athlete, I'm a competitor.

00:20:58.715 --> 00:21:01.218
I go out on a field and people
cheer when I make a play.

00:21:01.218 --> 00:21:04.221
And that's the best feeling in
sport that you can get right.

00:21:04.221 --> 00:21:05.055
Right.

00:21:05.055 --> 00:21:06.890
Going onto a stage like that,

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:09.559
staring out in an audience
and just hoping like hell

00:21:09.559 --> 00:21:11.812
I can make them laugh, was scary.

00:21:11.812 --> 00:21:12.813
But at the same time,

00:21:12.813 --> 00:21:14.064
once you do get that laugh,

00:21:14.064 --> 00:21:15.357
it's the exact same feeling

00:21:15.357 --> 00:21:17.526
as getting a sack or scoring a touchdown.

00:21:17.526 --> 00:21:19.736
Like there is no better feeling than that.

00:21:19.736 --> 00:21:20.570
No redos either.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.990
No. And it is live. And
you can't screw up, man.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:25.993
And it was so many
talented people around you

00:21:25.993 --> 00:21:27.786
and kind of, it's just like a team

00:21:27.786 --> 00:21:29.288
cause everybody's collaborating

00:21:29.288 --> 00:21:31.415
and everybody's trying to pull their line

00:21:31.415 --> 00:21:33.417
off the exact right way to get that laugh

00:21:33.417 --> 00:21:34.501
and to get that pop.

00:21:34.501 --> 00:21:36.670
And man, it was a really cool experience

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:38.880
and I hope I get to do it
again because I loved it.

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:42.426
And I realized that like live
performing to me is a blast.

00:21:42.426 --> 00:21:44.136
And I wish there's a way to work that in

00:21:44.136 --> 00:21:46.013
because I've really loved it.

00:21:46.013 --> 00:21:47.347
Well, you got a job right now

00:21:47.347 --> 00:21:48.849
that's live every time you play.

00:21:48.849 --> 00:21:52.436
So you stick with that for right now, man.

00:21:58.525 --> 00:22:01.653
So I read that you a huge fan of the EPL.

00:22:01.653 --> 00:22:02.487
Yeah, man.

00:22:02.487 --> 00:22:03.322
English Premier League.

00:22:03.322 --> 00:22:04.281
Yeah. I love it.

00:22:04.281 --> 00:22:05.532
Did you want to invest in it

00:22:05.532 --> 00:22:07.534
or something at some point? Ownership?

00:22:07.534 --> 00:22:08.910
It would be incredible.

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:12.080
But man, over there,
the soccer with money,

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:13.957
with how it all goes by,

00:22:13.957 --> 00:22:15.000
it's a different world over there.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.335
You go to Chelsea, right?

00:22:16.335 --> 00:22:17.169
Yeah, I'm a Chelsea guy.

00:22:17.169 --> 00:22:18.295
I started in 2011.

00:22:18.295 --> 00:22:19.838
Didier Drogba was at Chelsea,

00:22:19.838 --> 00:22:22.382
and I started getting
to the Premier League.

00:22:22.382 --> 00:22:24.509
I used to play with him
on Ivory Coast on FIFA,

00:22:24.509 --> 00:22:26.094
so I was like wherever
Didier is, I'm going.

00:22:26.094 --> 00:22:26.928
That would get you every time.

00:22:26.928 --> 00:22:28.722
Yeah. So yeah, I'm a big Chelsea fan,

00:22:28.722 --> 00:22:31.183
but man, it would be incredible
to invest over there,

00:22:31.183 --> 00:22:32.267
but as such with relegation...

00:22:32.267 --> 00:22:33.560
That's what makes it so exciting,

00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:35.062
is that you can get relegated.

00:22:35.062 --> 00:22:36.730
Imagine being dropped outta the NBA

00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:37.731
if you were in the bottom three.

00:22:37.731 --> 00:22:39.858
That, it's mind blowing.

00:22:39.858 --> 00:22:41.193
It is. It is.

00:22:41.193 --> 00:22:43.028
Which makes you have to be competitive.

00:22:43.028 --> 00:22:43.862
It's unbelievable.

00:22:43.862 --> 00:22:44.946
You have to stay competitive.

00:22:44.946 --> 00:22:46.740
And that's what keeps it so interesting.

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:49.368
And I don't even think a
model like that would...

00:22:49.368 --> 00:22:50.744
Nobody would let it happen over here,

00:22:50.744 --> 00:22:52.788
but that's what makes it
so exciting over there.

00:22:52.788 --> 00:22:54.039
That's super dope.

00:22:54.039 --> 00:22:55.248
I think that's why it was always dope

00:22:55.248 --> 00:22:57.709
in thinking about ownership

00:22:57.709 --> 00:22:59.753
with athletes or whatnot
cause you know what it takes.

00:22:59.753 --> 00:23:00.587
You know what I mean?

00:23:00.587 --> 00:23:03.256
Not just from the performance
standpoint standpoint,

00:23:03.256 --> 00:23:04.341
but you know what it's like.

00:23:04.341 --> 00:23:05.884
The locker room needs to be like,

00:23:05.884 --> 00:23:06.760
coaches and everything.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:08.303
Right. Yeah.

00:23:08.303 --> 00:23:10.430
You gonna be an owner someday?

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:11.723
I would love to.

00:23:11.723 --> 00:23:14.684
I would love to be a governor
of one of these teams.

00:23:14.684 --> 00:23:15.977
That's a goal of mine.

00:23:18.897 --> 00:23:20.023
Man, I appreciate you again, man.

00:23:20.023 --> 00:23:20.857
I appreciate you, brother .

00:23:20.857 --> 00:23:21.691
You know it .

00:23:21.691 --> 00:23:22.526
We'll catch up soon.

00:23:22.526 --> 00:23:23.360
Thank you so much, JJ.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.194
Thank you. I appreciate it.

00:23:24.194 --> 00:23:25.028
I really appreciate it.

00:23:25.028 --> 00:23:26.279
See you soon.

